    ["s0181","idiomatic","The civil track had relied only on Left Secretariat recommendations. In Huangtong 8 (1148) provincial ministers said, \"If we only follow the old precedent for recommendations, in time good and bad will not be distinguished and opportunism will multiply.\"","The civil track had relied only on Left Secretariat recommendations. In Emperor Xizong's Huangtong 8 (1148) provincial ministers said, \"If we only follow the old precedent for recommendations, in time good and bad will not be distinguished and opportunism will multiply.\"","s0181 has 至熙宗皇統八年; the idiomatic omits 熙宗, and restoring \"Emperor Xizong's\" before Huangtong 8 is accurate and natural.","high","applied"],
    ["s0163","idiomatic","In Dading 29 (1189) those who reached Pacifier of the Realm required an imperial order for further promotion.","In Zhangzong's Dading 29 (1189) those who reached Pacifier of the Realm required an imperial order for further promotion.","s0163 opens 章宗大定二十九年, so the omitted ruler must be restored; but 取旨升除 means promotions require obtaining an imperial order, and the proposal's \"received…thereafter\" wrongly softens that procedural force—keep the original \"required…for further promotion.\"","high","applied"]
